  "goodToKnow": "Die Mehrzahl means the majority: die Mehrzahl der Deutschen. In grammar, it's the native word for plural, and die Einzahl is the singular; school textbooks use these alongside Plural and Singular. For votes and elections, though, die Mehrheit is the usual word for majority: die absolute Mehrheit. German plural forms are notoriously varied: Häuser, Hunde, Autos, Frauen, Lehrer, so always learn a noun with its Mehrzahl."
